quiz 3 | What's the chemical formula of table salt?
* NaCl
o KCl
o NaOH
o CaCl₂
= Sodium chloride.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which element has atomic number 1?
* Hydrogen
o Helium
o Lithium
o Carbon
= One proton.
> Next

quiz 3 | Pure water has a pH of about…
* 7
o 0
o 14
o 5
= Neutral at 25°C.
> Next

quiz 3 | What gas do plants absorb for photosynthesis?
* Carbon dioxide
o Oxygen
o Nitrogen
o Hydrogen
= They release oxygen.
> Next

quiz 3 | Diamond is made of…
* Carbon
o Silicon
o Quartz
o Boron
= The same element as graphite and coal.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which metal is liquid at room temperature?
* Mercury
o Gallium
o Sodium
o Lead
= Gallium melts at about 30°C, just above typical room temperature.
> Next

quiz 4 | Avogadro's number is approximately…
* 6.02 × 10²³
o 3 × 10⁸
o 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹
o 9.8
= Particles per mole.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which element is the most abundant in the universe by mass?
* Hydrogen
o Helium
o Oxygen
o Carbon
= About 74% of normal matter by mass. Helium about 24%.
> Quick-fire round two complete
